Sokoban has either a BoH or an amulet of reflection. Should be in the
small room with the E-word engraved. But some monsters do not respect it
and may have grabed the object, so you should better search the whole zoo
for the stuff (and I guees you'll be able to know if it's a BoH or an
amulet easilly).

Concerning strategy, it depends on many things... Sokoban/Minetown are
mainly a matter of taste, you should do both but the order is not very
important. I usually go for Soko first if I happen to found an early altar
or to minetown first if I really need an altar and some price-iding. Also
depends on the light in the caves. If the first level(s) of the cave are
lit, I usually go down (a good way to make quite experience with fighting
classes, i find gnomes easy to kill).

Minesend usually go after both Soko and Minetown (making sometime rather
long trip between minetown/soko/minetwon/minsend).

Then i start going down, the Quest and ludios depend on whether I "feel"
it or not... I usually try to got lots of HPs (via alchemy) before the
Quest.

I also often take time to dig through the upper level even before I reach
Medusa, just because thatmakes a little change in the game and could be a
nice way to combine a camp movement with something else. But it is often a
source of YASD...

